{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-119464",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Since both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{11}-\\frac{9}{11}=\\frac{4-9}{11}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $4-9$ using a number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14148354/assets/3f5b60548cfd0332c74508678de51481f9fa149466c7d7880217b905e4d3891a.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{4-9}{11}=\\frac{-5}{11}=-\\frac{5}{11}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
